{
  "dom_id": "step-q35988",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Given  $f(x,y)=\\frac{3x+2y}{x-y}$, find $∇f(x,y).$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{3x+2y}{x-y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3(x-y)-(3x+2y)}{(x-y)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5y}{(x-y)^{2}} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{3x+2y}{x-y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x-y)+(3x+2y)}{(x-y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5x}{(x-y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\text{ }i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =-\\frac{5y}{(x-y)^{2}}\\text{ }i+\\frac{5x}{(x-y)^{2}}\\text{ }j \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{(x-y)^{2}}\\text{ }(y\\text{ }i-x\\text{ }j)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
